{"title":"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><ol><li>This is a twenty question free-response test. Each question has exactly one integer answer.</li>\n<li>You have 50 minutes to complete the test.</li>\n<li>You will receive 3 points for each correct answer, and 0 points for each problem left unanswered or incorrect.</li>\n<li>Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li>No aids are permitted other than scratch paper, graph paper, rulers, and erasers. No calculators, smartwatches, or computing devices are allowed. No problems on the test will require the use of a calculator.</li></ol>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3fdf734d37afcd7368b2c7eb50c8b46737b70c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{9}\\right)(3+6+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"201\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Brady has an unlimited supply of quarters (\\$0.25), dimes (\\$0.10), nickels (\\$0.05), and pennies (\\$0.01). What is the least number (quantity, not type) of coins Brady can use to pay off \\$<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28ce3117d645ae19c90d2f1bda739d458ddd4ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If all angles marked with a red square are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and all angles marked with one black curve are equal, find the measure of the angle with a question mark.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0b/Sprint4.png/400px-Sprint4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0b/Sprint4.png/600px-Sprint4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0b/Sprint4.png/800px-Sprint4.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A standard chess-board is an 8 by 8 grid of squares. A bishop is placed at square C5 (row 5, column C) and a rook is placed at square E4 (row 4, column E). How many squares can be attacked by both the bishop and rook if they each take one move?\n</p><p><br />\n(The bishop can attack any square in the same diagonal as itself, including squares A7, F8, G1, D6, and so on. The rook can attack any square in the same row or column as itself, including squares E5, E8, E4, C4, and so on.)\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint5.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/63/Sprint5.png/300px-Sprint5.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"301\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/63/Sprint5.png/450px-Sprint5.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/63/Sprint5.png/600px-Sprint5.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What two-digit even number has digits that sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Luis has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> coins that are all either nickels or dimes. If the probability of randomly picking a nickel from these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> coins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dcccc274b4e2547d9843c1e54b62c045285bc0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"17\" height=\"37\" /> how much money does Luis have in dollars?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many sets of three circles are in the diagram below such that their centers lie on the same line and each circle in the set is adjacent to another circle in the set? (Assume that if the centers of three circles appear to be on the same line, then they are on the same line. For example, the three red shaded circles count as one such set.)\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint9.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9a/Sprint9.png/400px-Sprint9.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9a/Sprint9.png/600px-Sprint9.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9a/Sprint9.png/800px-Sprint9.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive two-digit numbers exist such that the product of its digits is not zero?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A machine cuts a piece of metal at a constant rate. After leaving the machine alone for twenty minutes, the metal has been split into six pieces. How many more minutes will it take until there are twenty pieces?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Serena gets a grade of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e126f0d41c904d37ba2c332347a24b75d4ac3066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> for her chapter test. She doesn't remember how many problems there were, but she remembers that there were at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> problems, each problem solved correctly was worth an equal amount of points, and she did not receive any points for an incorrect or skipped question. Find the sum of all the possible numbers of problems that the test could have had.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many numbers are in the finite sequence of consecutive perfect squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f9f1e62863b82d5548bc8d8a32e611c94449ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9, 16, 25, \\ldots , 2500?\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The solution to the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed9db48b03c05157efa90c97754b20619c1c0274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\sqrt{x \\sqrt{x}}=2^{63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"113\" height=\"35\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Grace places a pencil in a cylindrical cup and is surprised to see that it fits diagonally. The pencil is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units long and of negligible thickness. The cup is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units tall. The volume of the cup can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7b6b9d217194b2a79485901cdf525545aa5898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> cubic units. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint14.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e2/Sprint14.jpg/200px-Sprint14.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"217\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e2/Sprint14.jpg/300px-Sprint14.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e2/Sprint14.jpg/400px-Sprint14.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ari, Bryant, Chandler, and David each tell one truth and one lie.\n</p>\n<ol><li>Ari: Bryant is the tallest among the four of us.  Chandler is the shortest among the four of us.</li>\n<li>Bryant: Ari is the oldest in the room.  Ari is the shortest in the room.</li>\n<li>Chandler: David is taller than me.  David is older than me.</li>\n<li>David: Chandler told two truths. I am the oldest person in the room.</li></ol>\n<p>If the first name of the shortest person is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> letters long and the first name of the second-tallest person is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> letters long, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef88f85f18da47a5ec57b0e3ea1c544fa93ad9d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\times b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> (Assume that no two people share the same height and are born on the same day.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a68a79dd5391c3d3c1bbc933c4092382304592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{10}-5^{10}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a concave quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437e65d3735fb1dadf06a8dc9c3d588e451252d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/830de927bd8077aa97abc0e3829961d12711fe7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f4b4507bf7da7632a03a6d62c19598104054b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CD = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f965f3742b873500fc1e353c851c012e2837d603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=90^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint16.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/Sprint16.jpg/350px-Sprint16.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"283\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/Sprint16.jpg/525px-Sprint16.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/Sprint16.jpg/700px-Sprint16.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 16\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest positive multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c1231e0a53f15ef2e95c0afa2a2738e8f9a1ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1003$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> that has no zeros in its decimal representation?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 17\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347971a51bf91ecee0bf15b003f0c189d709bf2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8acfd7d5ee559262593701b8dbd02e43ad96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" /> find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 18\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As an April Fool’s prank, Sean hacks his teacher’s digital clock and switches each digit to a certain letter. Right now, the hacked clock displays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/057ac7412072d095c8310cbcb23289411134790f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{M:AT}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes later, it displays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c861a9c7af21a38154a0974658678aa4d53a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{A:TM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />. If no two digits represent the same letter, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584789ddd2de1b12e8c12fcfadc9f0c679fe713b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{A} \\times \\textbf{M}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />    \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 19\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, define the operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a7644ee3d0b1d85e40b4ffd2e26eff4e2532c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\Delta y = x^3+y^2+x+y.\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"19\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7888ec6e1cd3c45c7d43cf6d157a7cb515a06cb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\dfrac{257 \\Delta 256}{258}}.\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 20\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems\">2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Sprint Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063831\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 336/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8609/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    4.968      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    4.968      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21622:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 2026101